WEBVTT

00:01.260 --> 00:08.300
When love takes shape, 
what happens to that which remains?

00:09.020 --> 00:13.410
The homunculi wish to return to Solomon.

00:13.980 --> 00:16.920
Their impulse to love is pronounced.

00:17.360 --> 00:21.690
With no one to love, they've lost control.

00:21.690 --> 00:24.700
I see. Then what about Ba'al?

00:25.120 --> 00:27.530
Only his love has fled.

00:28.680 --> 00:33.250
Once awakened, his hatred and 
destruction will be unleashed.

00:34.120 --> 00:36.750
What happened to Ba'al's love?

00:37.110 --> 00:41.250
I wouldn't know. That is his core.

00:41.250 --> 00:44.280
Once he exhausts his mana, 
he will die on his own.

00:44.280 --> 00:47.270
I see. Poor thing.

00:47.960 --> 00:50.650
I wonder where he's run off to.

01:04.500 --> 01:12.800
<b>My Daughter Left the Nest and Returned an S-Rank Adventurer</b>

02:23.530 --> 02:28.960
<b>Episode 10 "Wriggling Malice"</b>

02:30.090 --> 02:32.850
Ange, if you want to become an adventurer...

02:43.080 --> 02:44.920
<i>I have to protect her.</i>

02:47.570 --> 02:49.570
All right! All done!

02:50.570 --> 02:51.840
Thank you.

02:54.450 --> 02:56.430
Good job, Ms. Yuri!

02:56.430 --> 02:58.770
I'll do yours, sister.

03:00.180 --> 03:02.270
Okay! I'd love that.

03:11.060 --> 03:12.900
<i>A little brother and sister...</i>

03:12.900 --> 03:14.090
There we go.

03:15.900 --> 03:19.500
I thought a braid would look good on you.

03:19.500 --> 03:23.550
Gosh, I'm kind of embarrassed,
 but it's lovely!

03:23.900 --> 03:26.040
Thank you, Char.

03:38.370 --> 03:40.060
Isn't this fun?

03:40.380 --> 03:43.080
Should we really be farting around like this?

03:44.260 --> 03:46.710
I'll protect both of you.

03:47.290 --> 03:49.660
You're safe with your big sister!

03:50.150 --> 03:52.320
You don't have to fight anymore.

03:56.410 --> 03:57.890
Shall we get lunch?

03:57.890 --> 04:01.150
Yeah! Byaku, what do you want to eat?

04:02.860 --> 04:05.130
Pick whatever you want.

04:05.770 --> 04:09.890
Jeez! Sister, Byaku's still sulking.

04:10.740 --> 04:13.110
She's completely domesticated you.

04:14.240 --> 04:15.600
Isn't this fun?

04:21.360 --> 04:22.830
Granny Maria!

04:23.800 --> 04:25.500
Mind if we sit here?

04:26.140 --> 04:28.440
Keep it down, will you?

04:28.800 --> 04:33.310
You don't often come into town.
 What's the occasion?

04:33.310 --> 04:35.720
I needed some ingredients.

04:36.320 --> 04:37.890
Who're the kids?

04:38.240 --> 04:40.190
My little sister and brother.

04:40.190 --> 04:40.890
What?

04:41.680 --> 04:45.270
I'm kidding. They're staying 
with me for certain reasons.

04:45.600 --> 04:49.080
The girl is Charlotte, and the boy is Byaku.

04:49.080 --> 04:50.860
Come on, say hello.

04:53.680 --> 04:56.570
The girl's got a lot of mana.

04:56.570 --> 04:59.570
The boy's has a strange quality to it.

04:59.980 --> 05:01.270
Who are you?

05:01.590 --> 05:02.650
Who knows?

05:03.990 --> 05:06.400
Impudent little brat.

05:06.400 --> 05:10.400
Well, try not to cast too many magic circles.

05:11.480 --> 05:13.400
I'm protecting myself from surprise attacks.

05:14.420 --> 05:18.860
Including a blinding effect in
automatic defenses isn't half bad.

05:18.860 --> 05:21.580
But I know you can do better.

05:22.010 --> 05:23.330
Mind your own business.

05:28.450 --> 05:35.300
The circle on your left is flat, 
but the one to your right is spherical.

05:35.300 --> 05:39.020
You could cast a triangular 
pyramid or cube on top of that.

05:39.020 --> 05:41.980
And not just the edges of one, either.

05:41.980 --> 05:45.010
If you don't box it in, 
people will sense your mana.

05:46.530 --> 05:50.830
Say, Granny, do you think you
 could teach Char some spells?

05:51.540 --> 05:52.280
What?

05:53.750 --> 05:56.800
Just having mana doesn't
 mean you have talent.

05:57.320 --> 05:59.940
I'd need to see what she's capable of.

06:00.590 --> 06:04.200
Could you show her magic for self-defense?

06:04.710 --> 06:06.930
I'm a tough teacher.

06:06.930 --> 06:09.350
I don't like half-hearted students.

06:10.120 --> 06:11.560
Then it's a deal!

06:28.610 --> 06:29.810
What's the matter?

06:30.590 --> 06:35.920
I'm not sure I should be having so much 
fun after the terrible things I did.

06:37.030 --> 06:39.000
Don't worry about it.

06:39.000 --> 06:41.270
Life is full of joy.

06:42.580 --> 06:44.590
Thank you, sister.

06:45.950 --> 06:47.790
You con artists!

06:47.790 --> 06:50.220
How dare you show your faces here!

06:51.110 --> 06:53.230
I-I'm sorry...

06:53.230 --> 06:55.850
Solomon, my ass! You tricked us!

06:55.850 --> 06:57.940
How're you gonna make up for it?

06:58.300 --> 07:02.740
We've already returned your money. 
Why are you still bothering us?

07:02.740 --> 07:05.860
Scum! You're not sorry at all.

07:06.490 --> 07:09.440
What? Mind your own business!

07:09.760 --> 07:12.310
I won't say they did nothing wrong,

07:12.800 --> 07:18.180
but adults should not find fault with
 repentant kids and bully them.

07:20.590 --> 07:23.060
Who do you think you're talking to, broad?

07:22.370 --> 07:24.300
What's the meaning of this?

07:25.100 --> 07:28.140
Aren't you ashamed to treat children so?

07:28.600 --> 07:31.470
Lady Vienna would be 
saddened by your behavior.

07:32.270 --> 07:33.810
What'd you say?

07:33.810 --> 07:37.440
Hey, we really shouldn't pick a fight 
with a sister of the Vienna cult.

07:38.630 --> 07:40.300
Now then, let us be off.

07:41.780 --> 07:43.320
Let's go, Char.

07:44.940 --> 07:46.810
Thank you, Ms. Rosetta.

07:46.810 --> 07:49.810
I'm just glad they didn't try to hurt you.

07:49.810 --> 07:51.190
Who do we have here?

07:53.050 --> 07:56.440
This is Charlotte, and this is Byaku.

07:56.440 --> 07:58.710
They're staying with me for reasons.

07:58.710 --> 08:00.530
I'm Rosetta.

08:00.530 --> 08:04.200
I'm a sister at the nearby church orphanage.

08:07.510 --> 08:09.340
Do they not like me?

08:10.080 --> 08:15.180
You can't be rude now, Char. She helped us.

08:15.180 --> 08:18.720
Besides, Ms. Rosetta is one 
of my potential mothers.

08:19.340 --> 08:21.970
You're still going on about that?

08:21.970 --> 08:23.270
I'm serious.

08:23.270 --> 08:24.230
Sheesh.

08:25.270 --> 08:29.560
You shouldn't be associating with 
a sister of the Vienna cult.

08:30.420 --> 08:32.830
Sounds like you had a bad experience.

08:32.830 --> 08:35.130
Would you be willing to tell me about it?

08:35.790 --> 08:37.740
I have nothing to say.

08:38.260 --> 08:41.690
The goddess's love illuminates the land.

08:41.690 --> 08:44.960
Guiding the lost is one 
of our responsibilities.

08:45.700 --> 08:51.690
Love?! If you were about love, 
my parents wouldn't have been killed!

08:58.010 --> 08:59.440
That must've been hard.

09:00.190 --> 09:03.930
I don't need pity from 
a sister of the Vienna cult.

09:04.630 --> 09:10.870
Some clergy use their status 
and influence to do bad things.

09:11.560 --> 09:16.730
But there are also those who devoutly 
offer prayers and live tranquil lives.

09:17.080 --> 09:20.380
The goddess doesn't abandon 
people like that.

09:20.910 --> 09:21.940
Liar!

09:22.230 --> 09:25.330
Day in and day out, we prayed,
 attended services,

09:25.330 --> 09:27.560
and gave thanks for our good fortune!

09:28.290 --> 09:33.950
So why didn't the goddess save
 my mother and father?!

09:34.340 --> 09:37.500
Why? Why?!

09:41.090 --> 09:43.220
Where do you think you're going?

09:44.730 --> 09:47.660
I'm sorry. Er, nothing's the matter.

09:47.660 --> 09:49.450
We were just talking.

09:49.450 --> 09:51.070
That won't do.

09:51.360 --> 09:54.420
Bad children must be punished—

09:54.420 --> 09:57.510
Must... be killed.

10:06.990 --> 10:08.130
Oh, no!

10:08.510 --> 10:10.470
Bad children...

10:11.380 --> 10:12.970
Wh-Why...

10:13.980 --> 10:15.640
Thank goodness...

10:17.340 --> 10:18.730
Ms. Rosetta!

10:18.730 --> 10:21.820
Damn! I didn't sense his presence at all.

10:21.820 --> 10:23.220
I've been a fool.

10:27.580 --> 10:29.350
Get a grip.

10:36.270 --> 10:38.860
This... This is all my fault.

10:38.860 --> 10:40.660
Pull yourself together, Char.

10:42.120 --> 10:45.580
Byaku, they're just being controlled.

10:46.040 --> 10:47.200
Don't kill them.

10:48.770 --> 10:51.100
Quit wasting time. Get out of here already.

10:51.100 --> 10:52.830
You're coming with us.

10:53.230 --> 10:54.070
What?

10:54.070 --> 10:56.960
I'll protect you. You don't 
have to fight anymore.

10:57.640 --> 10:58.920
Take Char with you.

11:01.190 --> 11:03.350
I need medicine! Quickly!

11:04.530 --> 11:06.420
Very well. Take her to the infirmary.

11:06.420 --> 11:07.840
Someone bring a stretcher!

11:11.120 --> 11:12.220
What are you doing?

11:12.220 --> 11:13.990
Soldiers have no business here!

11:22.950 --> 11:24.470
What's wrong with them?

11:24.470 --> 11:26.130
Something's not right.

11:26.130 --> 11:29.800
They're just being controlled. 
Don't kill them.

11:29.800 --> 11:31.410
Don't be ridiculous!

11:31.410 --> 11:33.000
What's happened?

11:33.000 --> 11:34.240
Ms. Yuri.

11:35.610 --> 11:37.890
Could you disable them?

11:38.140 --> 11:40.690
I'll look for whoever's controlling them.

11:50.260 --> 11:52.140
That's what you wanted, right?

11:52.730 --> 11:53.890
Exactly.

12:01.340 --> 12:03.280
I told you, you don't need to fight!

12:04.060 --> 12:06.540
I'm not letting you protect me.

12:06.540 --> 12:09.900
Ange, you need to find the caster quickly.

12:09.900 --> 12:10.910
That's right.

12:19.110 --> 12:19.920
They're up above.

12:29.620 --> 12:33.870
Lady Vienna, protect us from evil...

12:35.340 --> 12:37.930
That was a nasty trick, Inquisition.

12:44.430 --> 12:47.950
They're too weak to test her strength.

12:50.350 --> 12:52.620
I'll try again.

13:03.850 --> 13:06.830
We were able to stop Ms. Rosetta's bleeding.

13:06.830 --> 13:09.610
She should be fine with rest now.

13:09.610 --> 13:11.030
Good.

13:11.030 --> 13:12.610
That wasn't easy, you know?

13:13.430 --> 13:17.230
Thank you for your help earlier, Ms. Yuri.

13:17.630 --> 13:21.410
Don't mention it. We help each 
other out when we're in need.

13:23.360 --> 13:25.350
I'm going to cool my head.

13:26.140 --> 13:28.350
Could you hold down the fort?

13:29.060 --> 13:31.920
Sure. Don't be too hard on yourself.

13:31.920 --> 13:33.060
Thanks.

13:37.460 --> 13:40.760
<i>And here I thought I'd become
 more like my dad...</i>

13:42.890 --> 13:44.210
Pathetic.

13:45.620 --> 13:48.640
You even boasted we'd be safe with you, too.

13:49.640 --> 13:50.640
I'm sorry.

13:52.240 --> 13:56.010
What the? It creeps me out 
when you don't put up a fight.

13:56.400 --> 13:59.500
I let myself get carried away.

13:59.990 --> 14:03.210
I hadn't truly considered what 
it means to protect someone.

14:05.340 --> 14:07.840
What should I have done?

14:10.270 --> 14:12.280
You're just like that kid.

14:13.380 --> 14:14.540
What did you say?

14:14.850 --> 14:17.540
You keep saying it's your fault.

14:17.980 --> 14:20.060
Shouldering all the responsibility

14:20.060 --> 14:23.570
like the heroine of some 
tragedy must feel nice.

14:24.020 --> 14:25.560
That's not my intention.

14:25.890 --> 14:29.670
If you ask me, your wishy-washy 
behavior is no different.

14:30.140 --> 14:33.550
This is even worse than the irritating 
way you were acting before.

14:34.080 --> 14:36.550
But because I got swept up in—

14:37.390 --> 14:38.240
Wait.

14:44.880 --> 14:46.080
It's one of <i>them!</i>

14:53.560 --> 14:56.260
Insects... Kill...

15:02.130 --> 15:03.080
Run!

15:04.790 --> 15:05.840
In my way...

15:11.340 --> 15:14.850
You don't have to fight. I'll protect you.

15:20.110 --> 15:20.980
Come at me!

15:29.770 --> 15:31.910
Hey, knock that off!

15:31.910 --> 15:34.970
You think you can beat it 
fighting so recklessly?

15:34.970 --> 15:36.160
Shut up!

15:36.530 --> 15:38.550
I won't fail again.

15:39.200 --> 15:41.800
I'll protect everyone!

15:42.500 --> 15:47.300
So suicidally taking on all the burden
 is how you protect people?

15:47.300 --> 15:49.660
I've had enough of your vanity!

15:57.210 --> 15:58.690
Screw this.

16:00.430 --> 16:01.930
Do you have a death wish?!

16:03.260 --> 16:05.930
Are you saying I was wrong?!

16:05.930 --> 16:08.120
What are you talking about?!

16:08.120 --> 16:11.950
Just take a look at yourself 
after lecturing <i>me!</i>

16:12.830 --> 16:13.900
But...

16:22.500 --> 16:23.440
Byaku!

16:44.120 --> 16:46.410
No. At this rate...

16:47.270 --> 16:50.380
Ange, if you want to become an adventurer,

16:51.110 --> 16:54.870
you must learn to view yourself objectively.

16:56.340 --> 16:58.580
What am I doing?

16:58.910 --> 17:02.500
I kept saying I'd protect them, 
but I was blind.

17:03.060 --> 17:06.330
I failed to objectively see 
how overexcited I was.

17:08.740 --> 17:11.830
It's not feinting. 
Its movements are straightforward.

17:12.290 --> 17:16.570
Compared to my dad, 
it's hardly a challenging opponent.

17:30.090 --> 17:32.390
Byaku, let me handle the rest.

17:32.390 --> 17:33.940
Don't you call me that.

17:40.440 --> 17:42.590
Come on. I'll play with you.

17:45.460 --> 17:49.460
Oh, right. I had trouble 
cutting the last one, too.

18:21.190 --> 18:22.510
How was that?

18:23.210 --> 18:26.510
Your big sister took care of business, huh?

18:37.620 --> 18:41.400
Interesting. I could leave 
her be for a while, I see.

18:48.630 --> 18:50.240
Well, well...

18:50.240 --> 18:52.400
You should be dead.

18:53.740 --> 18:57.150
The Great Gray Mage must have grown foolish.

18:57.400 --> 18:59.660
Who's the fool, scumbag?

18:59.660 --> 19:02.040
This is my turf.

19:03.520 --> 19:08.180
You seem unwell. Can you finish 
me in your current state?

19:09.170 --> 19:10.640
Silence!

19:18.070 --> 19:19.920
Have you lost your touch, Maria?

19:19.920 --> 19:23.540
That was just a test! Don't get cocky!

19:31.200 --> 19:33.060
Black is night, silver is blood.

19:33.060 --> 19:35.820
Wavering flame and illuminating 
moonlight color all things...

19:47.190 --> 19:48.600
He fled.

19:49.980 --> 19:53.960
Now that I know he's involved, 
I can't ignore this.

19:54.620 --> 19:57.290
It's a pain, but I'll look into it.

20:04.000 --> 20:05.480
Ms. Rosetta!

20:06.140 --> 20:07.440
Where am I?

20:07.970 --> 20:08.980
Ow...

20:09.300 --> 20:11.740
Don't strain yourself. You're badly injured.

20:11.740 --> 20:13.980
Ange, how is the girl?

20:17.210 --> 20:20.230
I'm glad you're all right.

20:20.580 --> 20:22.480
You... You dummy!

20:22.480 --> 20:25.520
Why'd you do that after 
I said such cruel things?

20:27.160 --> 20:30.600
I wouldn't know. I'm a dummy, after all.

20:31.000 --> 20:34.000
I'm just so glad you're all right.

20:34.710 --> 20:38.990
I'm sorry. Thank you for saving me.

20:50.260 --> 20:51.740
Duncan, beard.

20:51.740 --> 20:55.240
Now, now. My beard isn't a toy.

20:55.910 --> 20:57.430
Grandpa, up.

20:59.330 --> 21:01.150
He's really taken a liking to you.

21:01.520 --> 21:05.270
The villagers have accepted him, too.

21:05.760 --> 21:07.920
Probably because of Ange.

21:08.920 --> 21:11.280
Kids are cute, aren't they?

21:11.280 --> 21:12.090
Yeah.

21:12.870 --> 21:16.040
Hey, Bel, you ever think 
about getting hitched?

21:16.930 --> 21:20.550
Hitched? I don't have anyone to marry.

21:20.550 --> 21:23.180
You've never been in love?

21:24.000 --> 21:25.040
No.

21:33.910 --> 21:35.490
What's with that smile?!

21:35.490 --> 21:37.090
Are you in love with someone?

21:37.090 --> 21:39.950
What?! You have a sweetheart?

21:39.950 --> 21:40.370
Uh...

21:40.370 --> 21:44.210
If there's anything I can do to
 thank you for letting me stay here...

21:44.210 --> 21:45.190
What?

21:45.770 --> 21:49.410
No way. There's nothing a dolt 
like you can do to help.

21:49.810 --> 21:53.960
Lady Mary, you're just as 
much of a dolt as I am!

21:53.960 --> 21:57.790
What was that? Say that again!

21:57.330 --> 22:00.690
<i>Percy, Kasim, and Satie...</i>

22:01.200 --> 22:03.150
<i>I wonder what they're up to now.</i>

23:35.060 --> 23:40.010
<b>Next Time</b>

23:35.060 --> 23:40.010
<b>"Belgrieve's Decision"</b>
